  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Which equation describes the set of all points $(x,y)$ in the coordinate plane that are a distance of $12$ units from the origin?",
  "worked_solution": "The set of all points $(x,y)$ that are a distance of $12$ units from the origin defines a circle with radius $r=12$ centered at the origin, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/ae57797a973213ad2b8050a937c449b83e8503c42d3fe5783ad23950a47c1046.png)\n\nSo, the required equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={12}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =144.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
